  "step_3": "The decision reason prioritizes higher probability of a favorable outcome and would favor Lottery B (25% vs 20%). However, the individual explicitly chooses the option with the lower probability (implied to be Lottery A) for the sake of a higher reward. The individual considers the probabilities but does not use them as a basis for preference in the way the reason dictates; instead, they trade off lower probability for higher payoff. There is no indication that differences in probabilities drove the choice toward the higher-probability option—in fact, the choice goes in the opposite direction. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the individual’s deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
